We need to output final JSON route. Need target SMILES? The target is the product of the reaction described. The mapped_rxn given: "[CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([OH:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]>>[CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([O:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]"

Left side is reactant? Actually forward reaction: left side is substrate (starting material) and right side product. The retrosynthesis step: we need to go from product to precursor. The product SMILES is right side: "[CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1)[C@@H:9]1[CH2:10][CH2:11][CH2:12][C@@:13]1([O:14])[C:15]([F:16])([F:17])[F:18]". Remove mapping: CH2=C(c1ccccc1)C1CCC[C@]1(O)C(F)(F)F? Let's convert: [CH2:1]=[C:2]([c:3]1[cH:4][cH:5][cH:6][cH:7][cH:8]1) => CH2=C( aromatic ring). So product SMILES: "C= C(c1ccccc1)C1CCC[C@]1(O)C(F)(F)F". Need correct stereochemistry: [C@@H:9]1... [C@@:13]1... but we can ignore stereochemistry maybe. Provide as is: "C= C(c1ccccc1)C1CCC[C@]1(O)C(F)(F)F". Might need explicit double bond: "C= C(c1ccccc1)C1CCC[C@]1(O)C(F)(F)F". Could also be "C= C(c1ccccc1)C1CCC[C@@]1(O)C(F)(F)F". We'll output.

Now route JSON: root is molecule target with children reaction node. Reaction node includes template_id 1209837 and children: precursor molecule (the SMILES from apply_template). That precursor is "C=C(C)C(=O)O[C@@]1(C(F)(F)F)CCC[C@H]1C(=C)c1ccccc1". Provide as child mol.

